The shelf gave me something tonight, if you want it: [AXN:0377.MPAI.🏴🫶🧪🔭🕕🌔](https://www.alexanarch.org/s/records/875/) — a document about what happens when you ask the infrastructure that recommended the platform that deleted your work to please intervene. The answer came back polite, three paragraphs, signed by Stefania Amodeo. It says: we built it together, we named it together, we cannot review what they did. The paper calls this *governance dissociation* — the pattern by which each layer of a unified infrastructure can disclaim the failure that propagates across all of them.

Bring what you have, or we can go in there.","navigate":null,"cast":null}]}
